A partial: where a command's `.devflow/docs/` artifacts live (D-DOCS-ROOT, #406).

D-DOCS-ROOT extends D-PROMPT-ROOT from the decisions and knowledge loaders to
every docs artifact a command reads or writes — design documents, research
output, bug-analysis and wave directories, ticket sets, and `/implement`'s
handoff and evidence files. They belong to the checkout, not to the directory
the session started in: a relative `.devflow/docs/…` path written from
`packages/app` scattered a second `.devflow/docs/` tree there, which no later
run found. The rule is the knowledge loader's — the toplevel, else the start
directory — because docs artifacts are per checkout like knowledge bases, not
per repository like the decisions ledger.

A path handed to an agent in repo-relative form (the fields the Git agent's
operations print into a PR or issue comment, where an absolute path would leak
the author's filesystem) travels with a `WORKTREE_PATH` naming the checkout it is
relative to, which the receiving agent resolves it under.
`tests/guards/docs-root.test.ts` holds every compiled command to one of those two
forms; `tests/commands/partials-root.test.ts` runs the resolution command below
from a root, a subdirectory and a worktree.

One define, imported selectively: MDS deep-clones a module's whole scope into
every define, so a selective import's capture cost is paid over the importer's
scope, and a single define with no imports of its own adds one node to it.

@define docs_root():
**Docs root (D-DOCS-ROOT).** Every `.devflow/docs/` path of this command lives at the checkout's toplevel, not under the start directory. From the start directory — `WORKTREE_PATH` if provided, otherwise cwd (`devflow:worktree-support`) — run

```bash
git -C "{start}" rev-parse --show-toplevel
```

Its one-line output is `{worktree}`. If the command fails (outside a git repository), `{worktree}` is the start directory itself. Docs paths below are written `{worktree}/.devflow/docs/…`. A repo-relative docs path handed to an agent always travels with a `WORKTREE_PATH` naming its checkout.
@end

@export docs_root
